.SH "NAME"
neonrelay \- starts the Neon Relay client
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBneonrelay\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]\&... [\-f \fICONFIG_FILE\fR]\&...
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Neon Relay is a cooperative 2D platform/race game with an optional reward rail for
Solana Mobile (Seeker) players\&. It is a standalone derivative of the upstream DDNet
project, which is itself an actively maintained version of \fBDDRace\fR, a
\fBTeeworlds\fR modification\&. See \fIUPSTREAM_BASE\&.md\fR and \fIlicense\&.txt\fR in
the repository for the exact upstream commit and for attribution\&.
.sp
Rewards are decided by the game server and the reward service, never by the client\&.
Connecting a wallet is optional; the game is fully playable without one\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-f\fR \fICONFIGURATION_FILE\fR
.RS 4
Load
\fICONFIGURATION_FILE\fR
instead of the default
\fIsettings_neonrelay\&.cfg\fR\&. Can be given multiple times; later files override
earlier ones\&.
.RE
.sp
All other options are configuration variables\&. They are documented in\-game under
Settings and in
\fIsrc/engine/shared/config_variables\&.h\fR\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
neonrelay \-f myfile\&.cfg
neonrelay \-f myfile\&.cfg \-f myfile2\&.cfg
neonrelay \*(Aqcl_showhud 0\*(Aq \*(Aqplayer_name "nameless tee"\*(Aq
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.SH "FILES"
.PP
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/NeonRelay\fR (or \fI~/Library/Application Support/NeonRelay\fR,
\fI%APPDATA%/NeonRelay\fR)
.RS 4
User directory: settings, downloaded maps, demos, screenshots\&. Existing
\fIDDNet\fR
and
\fITeeworlds\fR
directories are reused if the Neon Relay directory does not exist yet\&.
.RE
